From b3acdd43ac376df426ca0f9a0bdba0a5ca7e24f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Ceccarelli Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 18:32:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(v8): truck/container load calculator + /tools hub,
 on a shared packer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extracts the layer-pattern search from lib/palletize.ts into lib/rectpack.ts
(column / two-block / four-block enumeration over any region and item), then
reuses it for vehicle loading: cases on a deck and pallets on a trailer floor
are the same geometry problem. Pallet solver output is unchanged — verified
against the original test vectors.

- lib/truckload.ts: vehicle presets (13.6 m curtainsider, rigid, 20/40 ft,
  40 ft HC, box van), double-stacking gated on interior height, payload limit,
  and an explicit 'limited by space vs payload' verdict
- /tools/truck-load-calculator (en + de): plan view, CSV load plan, SSR method
  and FAQ, SoftwareApplication + FAQPage + BreadcrumbList schema
- /tools hub (en + de) as a crawlable parent; nav and home band now point there
- Cross-links both ways: cases -> pallets -> vehicle
- Cross-checked against canonical freight figures: 20 ft = 11 EUR pallets,
  40 ft = 25, 13.6 m trailer = 34 floor spots (the FAQ explains 33 vs 34)
- Disclaimer names what is NOT modelled: EN 12195 securing, axle loads,
  dangerous goods, door clearance

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
